{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והנשיאים", :translit "ve-ha-nesi'im", :gloss "and the princes"} {:he "נשיא משבט", :translit "nasi mi-shevet", :gloss "a prince of the tribe"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Phinehas led the campaign alone, without the standard tribal princes, to spare Simeon the embarrassment of having lost its prince Zimri in the sin of Peor."}], :frame {:text "The sin of Ba'al Peor involved Zimri son of Salu, a prince of a Simeonite ancestral house, who was killed by Phinehas son of Eleazar (Numbers 25:14). The tribal princes, one per tribe, are enumerated earlier (Numbers 1:5–16) and served as the standard leadership; their absence here is thus conspicuous.", :sources ["Numbers 25:14" "Numbers 1:5-16"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Phinehas led the campaign alone, without the standard tribal princes, to spare Simeon the embarrassment of having lost its prince Zimri in the sin of Peor.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:09.313730001Z", :model "glm-5.2"}